    ///   division for three components) instead of the `scale.recip()` then `column *
    ///   inv_scale` of glam-rs, which rounds twice. Each length is the floor of the exact
    ///   one, so a normalized column is within `1 / scale` ULP per component.
    /// * The rotation is `Quat::from_rotation_axes` of the normalized columns: its own
    ///   error (a square root and a shared division) adds to the above. Measured over 20
    ///   000 random `(scale, rotation, translation)` triples of the Python mirror, the
    ///   round trip `to_scale_rotation_translation(from_scale_rotation_translation(..))`
    ///   recovers the translation exactly, the rotation within 13 raw ULP per component
    ///   and the scale within `5 |scale| + 2` ULP, the linear term being the drift of the
    ///   squared length of the quantized quaternion.
    fn to_scale_rotation_translation(self: Mat4) -> (Vec3, Quat, Vec3);
    /// Creates an affine transformation matrix containing a 3D rotation around a
    /// normalized rotation `axis` of `angle` (in radians).
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::from_axis_angle`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * The `glam_assert!` precondition is not checked (docs/DESIGN.md section 3). `axis`
    ///   must be normalized.
    /// * `fixed::trig::sin_cos` is accurate to about 1 ULP over a turn (see its
    ///   documentation); the products that follow add one floor rescale each.
    /// * Every element is one exact triple product plus one exact term, rescaled once
    ///   (floored).
    fn from_axis_angle(axis: Vec3, angle: Fixed) -> Mat4;
    /// Creates an affine transformation matrix containing a 3D rotation around the x axis
    /// of `angle` (in radians).
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::from_rotation_x`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * Never.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * `fixed::trig::sin_cos` is accurate to about 1 ULP over a turn (see its
    ///   documentation); the products that follow add one floor rescale each.
    fn from_rotation_x(angle: Fixed) -> Mat4;
    /// Creates an affine transformation matrix containing a 3D rotation around the y axis
    /// of `angle` (in radians).
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::from_rotation_y`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * Never.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * `fixed::trig::sin_cos` is accurate to about 1 ULP over a turn (see its
    ///   documentation); the products that follow add one floor rescale each.
    fn from_rotation_y(angle: Fixed) -> Mat4;
    /// Creates an affine transformation matrix containing a 3D rotation around the z axis
    /// of `angle` (in radians).
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::from_rotation_z`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * Never.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * `fixed::trig::sin_cos` is accurate to about 1 ULP over a turn (see its
    ///   documentation); the products that follow add one floor rescale each.
    fn from_rotation_z(angle: Fixed) -> Mat4;
    /// Transforms the given 3D vector as a point.
    ///
    /// This is the equivalent of multiplying the 3D vector as a 4D vector where `w` is
    /// `1`.
    ///
    /// This method assumes that `self` contains a valid affine transform. It does not
    /// perform a perspective divide: use `project_point3` for a projective transform.
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::transform_point3`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * The `glam_assert!` precondition is not checked (docs/DESIGN.md section 3). The
    ///   4th row of `self` must be `(0, 0, 0, 1)`.
    /// * One `dot3_add` fused kernel per element: the translation is added exactly inside
    ///   the single rescale, so the result is at most 1 ULP below the exact value.
    fn transform_point3(self: Mat4, rhs: Vec3) -> Vec3;
    /// Transforms the given 3D vector as a direction.
    ///
    /// This is the equivalent of multiplying the 3D vector as a 4D vector where `w` is
    /// `0`.
    ///
    /// This method assumes that `self` contains a valid affine transform.
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::transform_vector3`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * The `glam_assert!` precondition is not checked (docs/DESIGN.md section 3). The
    ///   4th row of `self` must be `(0, 0, 0, 1)`.
    /// * One `dot3` fused kernel per element of the result: the exact Q64.64 sum of the 3
    ///   products is rescaled once (floored), so no intermediate term can overflow and the
    ///   element is at most 1 ULP below the exact value.
    fn transform_vector3(self: Mat4, rhs: Vec3) -> Vec3;
    /// Transforms the given 3D vector as a point, applying perspective correction.
    ///
    /// This is the equivalent of multiplying the 3D vector as a 4D vector where `w` is
    /// `1`. The perspective divide is performed, meaning the resulting 3D vector is
    /// divided by `w`.
    ///
    /// This method assumes that `self` contains a projective transform.
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::project_point3`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Fixed: division by zero'` if the projected `w` is zero.
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * One division shared by the three components (`Recip`, rounded to nearest) instead
    ///   of the three of `res / res.w`.
    /// * Each numerator is one `dot3_add` fused kernel (one floor rescale), so the result
    ///   is within `1 / |w|` ULP of the exact projection plus the rounding of the shared
    ///   division.
    fn project_point3(self: Mat4, rhs: Vec3) -> Vec3;
    /// Creates a right-handed view matrix using a camera position, a facing direction and
    /// an up direction.
    ///
    /// For a view coordinate system with `+X=right`, `+Y=up` and `+Z=back`.
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::look_to_rh`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Vec3: normalize zero'` if `dir` and `up` are parallel.
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// * `'i64_neg Underflow'` if an element is `MIN`.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * The `glam_assert!` precondition is not checked (docs/DESIGN.md section 3). `dir`
    ///   and `up` must be normalized.
    /// * Deprecated in glam-rs 0.33.1 in favour of `glam::camera`, which is not ported yet
    ///   (task C1 of `docs/PLAN.md`); the name and the layout are the ones of
    ///   `Mat4::look_to_rh`.
    /// * `s` is normalized (one square root, one shared division, rounded to nearest) and
    ///   every other element is exact or one floored `dot3`.
    fn look_to_rh(eye: Vec3, dir: Vec3, up: Vec3) -> Mat4;
    /// Creates a left-handed view matrix using a camera position, a facing direction and
    /// an up direction.
    ///
    /// For a view coordinate system with `+X=right`, `+Y=up` and `+Z=forward`.
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::look_to_lh`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Vec3: normalize zero'` if `dir` and `up` are parallel.
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// * `'i64_neg Underflow'` if an element is `MIN`.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * The `glam_assert!` precondition is not checked (docs/DESIGN.md section 3). `dir`
    ///   and `up` must be normalized.
    /// * Deprecated in glam-rs 0.33.1 in favour of `glam::camera`, which is not ported yet
    ///   (task C1 of `docs/PLAN.md`); the name and the layout are the ones of
    ///   `Mat4::look_to_rh`.
    /// * `s` is normalized (one square root, one shared division, rounded to nearest) and
    ///   every other element is exact or one floored `dot3`.
    fn look_to_lh(eye: Vec3, dir: Vec3, up: Vec3) -> Mat4;
    /// Creates a right-handed view matrix using a camera position, a focal point and an up
    /// direction.
    ///
    /// For a view coordinate system with `+X=right`, `+Y=up` and `+Z=back`.
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::look_at_rh`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Vec3: normalize zero'` if `center` is `eye`, or if the direction and `up` are
    ///   parallel.
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// * `'i64_neg Underflow'` if an element is `MIN`.
    /// * `'i64_sub Overflow'` / `'i64_sub Underflow'` if an element difference leaves the
    ///   scalar range.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * The `glam_assert!` precondition is not checked (docs/DESIGN.md section 3). `dir`
    ///   and `up` must be normalized.
    /// * Deprecated in glam-rs 0.33.1 in favour of `glam::camera`, which is not ported yet
    ///   (task C1 of `docs/PLAN.md`); the name and the layout are the ones of
    ///   `Mat4::look_to_rh`.
    /// * `s` is normalized (one square root, one shared division, rounded to nearest) and
    ///   every other element is exact or one floored `dot3`.
    fn look_at_rh(eye: Vec3, center: Vec3, up: Vec3) -> Mat4;
    /// Creates a left-handed view matrix using a camera position, a focal point and an up
    /// direction.
    ///
    /// For a view coordinate system with `+X=right`, `+Y=up` and `+Z=forward`.
    ///
    /// Mirrors `glam::Mat4::look_at_lh`.
    /// #### Panics
    /// * `'Vec3: normalize zero'` if `center` is `eye`, or if the direction and `up` are
    ///   parallel.
    /// * `'Fixed: overflow'` if the result does not fit the scalar range.
    /// * `'i64_neg Underflow'` if an element is `MIN`.
    /// * `'i64_sub Overflow'` / `'i64_sub Underflow'` if an element difference leaves the
    ///   scalar range.
    /// #### Deviations
    /// * The `glam_assert!` precondition is not checked (docs/DESIGN.md section 3). `dir`
    ///   and `up` must be normalized.
    /// * Deprecated in glam-rs 0.33.1 in favour of `glam::camera`, which is not ported yet
    ///   (task C1 of `docs/PLAN.md`); the name and the layout are the ones of
    ///   `Mat4::look_to_rh`.
    /// * `s` is normalized (one square root, one shared division, rounded to nearest) and
    ///   every other element is exact or one floored `dot3`.
    fn look_at_lh(eye: Vec3, center: Vec3, up: Vec3) -> Mat4;
}

pub impl Mat4Impl of Mat4Trait {
    const ZERO: Mat4 = Mat4 {
        x_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0 }, y: Fixed { raw: 0 }, z: Fixed { raw: 0 }, w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
        },
        y_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0 }, y: Fixed { raw: 0 }, z: Fixed { raw: 0 }, w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
        },
        z_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0 }, y: Fixed { raw: 0 }, z: Fixed { raw: 0 }, w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
        },
        w_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0 }, y: Fixed { raw: 0 }, z: Fixed { raw: 0 }, w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
        },
    };
    const IDENTITY: Mat4 = Mat4 {
        x_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0x100000000 },
            y: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            z: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
        },
        y_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            y: Fixed { raw: 0x100000000 },
            z: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
        },
        z_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            y: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            z: Fixed { raw: 0x100000000 },
            w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
        },
        w_axis: Vec4 {
            x: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            y: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            z: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            w: Fixed { raw: 0x100000000 },
        },
    };

    #[inline(always)]
    fn from_cols(x_axis: Vec4, y_axis: Vec4, z_axis: Vec4, w_axis: Vec4) -> Mat4 {
        Mat4 { x_axis, y_axis, z_axis, w_axis }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn from_rows(row0: Vec4, row1: Vec4, row2: Vec4, row3: Vec4) -> Mat4 {
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Vec4 { x: row0.x, y: row1.x, z: row2.x, w: row3.x },
            y_axis: Vec4 { x: row0.y, y: row1.y, z: row2.y, w: row3.y },
            z_axis: Vec4 { x: row0.z, y: row1.z, z: row2.z, w: row3.z },
            w_axis: Vec4 { x: row0.w, y: row1.w, z: row2.w, w: row3.w },
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn from_cols_array(m: [Fixed; 16]) -> Mat4 {
        let [m00, m01, m02, m03, m10, m11, m12, m13, m20, m21, m22, m23, m30, m31, m32, m33] = m;
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Vec4 { x: m00, y: m01, z: m02, w: m03 },
            y_axis: Vec4 { x: m10, y: m11, z: m12, w: m13 },
            z_axis: Vec4 { x: m20, y: m21, z: m22, w: m23 },
            w_axis: Vec4 { x: m30, y: m31, z: m32, w: m33 },
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn to_cols_array(self: Mat4) -> [Fixed; 16] {
        [
            self.x_axis.x, self.x_axis.y, self.x_axis.z, self.x_axis.w, self.y_axis.x,
            self.y_axis.y, self.y_axis.z, self.y_axis.w, self.z_axis.x, self.z_axis.y,
            self.z_axis.z, self.z_axis.w, self.w_axis.x, self.w_axis.y, self.w_axis.z,
            self.w_axis.w,
        ]
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn from_rows_array(m: [Fixed; 16]) -> Mat4 {
        let [m00, m01, m02, m03, m10, m11, m12, m13, m20, m21, m22, m23, m30, m31, m32, m33] = m;
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Vec4 { x: m00, y: m10, z: m20, w: m30 },
            y_axis: Vec4 { x: m01, y: m11, z: m21, w: m31 },
            z_axis: Vec4 { x: m02, y: m12, z: m22, w: m32 },
            w_axis: Vec4 { x: m03, y: m13, z: m23, w: m33 },
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn to_rows_array(self: Mat4) -> [Fixed; 16] {
        [
            self.x_axis.x, self.y_axis.x, self.z_axis.x, self.w_axis.x, self.x_axis.y,
            self.y_axis.y, self.z_axis.y, self.w_axis.y, self.x_axis.z, self.y_axis.z,
            self.z_axis.z, self.w_axis.z, self.x_axis.w, self.y_axis.w, self.z_axis.w,
            self.w_axis.w,
        ]
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn from_cols_array_2d(m: [[Fixed; 4]; 4]) -> Mat4 {
        let [x_axis, y_axis, z_axis, w_axis] = m;
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Vec4Trait::from_array(x_axis),
            y_axis: Vec4Trait::from_array(y_axis),
            z_axis: Vec4Trait::from_array(z_axis),
            w_axis: Vec4Trait::from_array(w_axis),
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn to_cols_array_2d(self: Mat4) -> [[Fixed; 4]; 4] {
        [
            [self.x_axis.x, self.x_axis.y, self.x_axis.z, self.x_axis.w],
            [self.y_axis.x, self.y_axis.y, self.y_axis.z, self.y_axis.w],
            [self.z_axis.x, self.z_axis.y, self.z_axis.z, self.z_axis.w],
            [self.w_axis.x, self.w_axis.y, self.w_axis.z, self.w_axis.w],
        ]
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn from_diagonal(diagonal: Vec4) -> Mat4 {
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Vec4 {
                x: diagonal.x, y: Fixed { raw: 0 }, z: Fixed { raw: 0 }, w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            },
            y_axis: Vec4 {
                x: Fixed { raw: 0 }, y: diagonal.y, z: Fixed { raw: 0 }, w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            },
            z_axis: Vec4 {
                x: Fixed { raw: 0 }, y: Fixed { raw: 0 }, z: diagonal.z, w: Fixed { raw: 0 },
            },
            w_axis: Vec4 {
                x: Fixed { raw: 0 }, y: Fixed { raw: 0 }, z: Fixed { raw: 0 }, w: diagonal.w,
            },
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn diagonal(self: Mat4) -> Vec4 {
        Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.x, y: self.y_axis.y, z: self.z_axis.z, w: self.w_axis.w }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn col(self: Mat4, index: usize) -> Vec4 {
        match index {
            0 => self.x_axis,
            1 => self.y_axis,
            2 => self.z_axis,
            3 => self.w_axis,
            _ => core::panic_with_felt252('Mat4: index out of bounds'),
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn row(self: Mat4, index: usize) -> Vec4 {
        match index {
            0 => Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.x, y: self.y_axis.x, z: self.z_axis.x, w: self.w_axis.x },
            1 => Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.y, y: self.y_axis.y, z: self.z_axis.y, w: self.w_axis.y },
            2 => Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.z, y: self.y_axis.z, z: self.z_axis.z, w: self.w_axis.z },
            3 => Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.w, y: self.y_axis.w, z: self.z_axis.w, w: self.w_axis.w },
            _ => core::panic_with_felt252('Mat4: index out of bounds'),
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn transpose(self: Mat4) -> Mat4 {
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.x, y: self.y_axis.x, z: self.z_axis.x, w: self.w_axis.x },
            y_axis: Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.y, y: self.y_axis.y, z: self.z_axis.y, w: self.w_axis.y },
            z_axis: Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.z, y: self.y_axis.z, z: self.z_axis.z, w: self.w_axis.z },
            w_axis: Vec4 { x: self.x_axis.w, y: self.y_axis.w, z: self.z_axis.w, w: self.w_axis.w },
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn determinant(self: Mat4) -> Fixed {
        let coef00 = mul_sub(self.z_axis.z, self.w_axis.w, self.w_axis.z, self.z_axis.w);
        let coef04 = mul_sub(self.z_axis.y, self.w_axis.w, self.w_axis.y, self.z_axis.w);
        let coef08 = mul_sub(self.z_axis.y, self.w_axis.z, self.w_axis.y, self.z_axis.z);
        let coef12 = mul_sub(self.z_axis.x, self.w_axis.w, self.w_axis.x, self.z_axis.w);
        let coef16 = mul_sub(self.z_axis.x, self.w_axis.z, self.w_axis.x, self.z_axis.z);
        let coef20 = mul_sub(self.z_axis.x, self.w_axis.y, self.w_axis.x, self.z_axis.y);
        let q0 = wide_mul(self.y_axis.y, coef00)
            .sub(wide_mul(self.y_axis.z, coef04))
            .add(wide_mul(self.y_axis.w, coef08));
        let q1 = wide_mul(self.y_axis.z, coef12)
            .sub(wide_mul(self.y_axis.x, coef00))
            .sub(wide_mul(self.y_axis.w, coef16));
        let q2 = wide_mul(self.y_axis.x, coef04)
            .sub(wide_mul(self.y_axis.y, coef12))
            .add(wide_mul(self.y_axis.w, coef20));
        let q3 = wide_mul(self.y_axis.y, coef16)
            .sub(wide_mul(self.y_axis.x, coef08))
            .sub(wide_mul(self.y_axis.z, coef20));
        q0
            .mul(self.x_axis.x)
            .add(q1.mul(self.x_axis.y))
            .add(q2.mul(self.x_axis.z))
            .add(q3.mul(self.x_axis.w))
            .narrow()
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn mul_vec4(self: Mat4, rhs: Vec4) -> Vec4 {
        Vec4 {
            x: dot4(
                self.x_axis.x,
                rhs.x,
                self.y_axis.x,
                rhs.y,
                self.z_axis.x,
                rhs.z,
                self.w_axis.x,
                rhs.w,
            ),
            y: dot4(
                self.x_axis.y,
                rhs.x,
                self.y_axis.y,
                rhs.y,
                self.z_axis.y,
                rhs.z,
                self.w_axis.y,
                rhs.w,
            ),
            z: dot4(
                self.x_axis.z,
                rhs.x,
                self.y_axis.z,
                rhs.y,
                self.z_axis.z,
                rhs.z,
                self.w_axis.z,
                rhs.w,
            ),
            w: dot4(
                self.x_axis.w,
                rhs.x,
                self.y_axis.w,
                rhs.y,
                self.z_axis.w,
                rhs.z,
                self.w_axis.w,
                rhs.w,
            ),
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn mul_transpose_vec4(self: Mat4, rhs: Vec4) -> Vec4 {
        Vec4 {
            x: dot4(
                self.x_axis.x,
                rhs.x,
                self.x_axis.y,
                rhs.y,
                self.x_axis.z,
                rhs.z,
                self.x_axis.w,
                rhs.w,
            ),
            y: dot4(
                self.y_axis.x,
                rhs.x,
                self.y_axis.y,
                rhs.y,
                self.y_axis.z,
                rhs.z,
                self.y_axis.w,
                rhs.w,
            ),
            z: dot4(
                self.z_axis.x,
                rhs.x,
                self.z_axis.y,
                rhs.y,
                self.z_axis.z,
                rhs.z,
                self.z_axis.w,
                rhs.w,
            ),
            w: dot4(
                self.w_axis.x,
                rhs.x,
                self.w_axis.y,
                rhs.y,
                self.w_axis.z,
                rhs.z,
                self.w_axis.w,
                rhs.w,
            ),
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn mul_mat4(self: Mat4, rhs: Mat4) -> Mat4 {
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Self::mul_vec4(self, rhs.x_axis),
            y_axis: Self::mul_vec4(self, rhs.y_axis),
            z_axis: Self::mul_vec4(self, rhs.z_axis),
            w_axis: Self::mul_vec4(self, rhs.w_axis),
        }
    }

    #[inline(always)]
    fn add_mat4(self: Mat4, rhs: Mat4) -> Mat4 {
        Mat4 {
            x_axis: Vec4 {
                x: self.x_axis.x + rhs.x_axis.x,
                y: self.x_axis.y + rhs.x_axis.y,
                z: self.x_axis.z + rhs.x_axis.z,
                w: self.x_axis.w + rhs.x_axis.w,
            },
            y_axis: Vec4 {
                x: self.y_axis.x + rhs.y_axis.x,
                y: self.y_axis.y + rhs.y_axis.y,
                z: self.y_axis.z + rhs.y_axis.z,
                w: self.y_axis.w + rhs.y_axis.w,
            },
            z_axis: Vec4 {
                x: self.z_axis.x + rhs.z_axis.x,
                y: self.z_axis.y + rhs.z_axis.y,
                z: self.z_axis.z + rhs.z_axis.z,
                w: self.z_axis.w + rhs.z_axis.w,
            },
            w_axis: Vec4 {
                x: self.w_axis.x + rhs.w_axis.x,
                y: self.w_axis.y + rhs.w_axis.y,
                z: self.w_axis.z + rhs.w_axis.z,
                w: self.w_axis.w + rhs.w_axis.w,
            },
